menu "Rollo"

    config ROLLO_TRAVEL_UP_MS
        int "Run time from fully down to fully up (ms)"
        default 30000
        help
            There is no encoder: the position comes from the motor's run time. Time a full
            run up once and enter it here.

    config ROLLO_TRAVEL_DOWN_MS
        int "Run time from fully up to fully down (ms)"
        default 30000
        help
            Time a full run down once and enter it here. It can differ from the run up
            (the bottom bar pulls with it going down); if it doesn't, enter the same time.

    config ROLLO_VIRTUAL_MAX_PERCENT
        int "Virtual fully down (% of the full run down)"
        range 1 100
        default 100
        help
            Where "fully closed" is, as a share of the full height timed above. With 80,
            closing stops at 80 % of the full run, and Matter's 0-100 % spans only that
            range: 50 % is 40 % of the full height. Change it without measuring the travel
            times again; the saved position stays where the blind really is.

    config ROLLO_JOG_MS
        int "Jog run time (ms)"
        range 50 10000
        default 1000
        help
            How long the jog up / jog down switches run the motor. A jog ignores fully up
            and the virtual fully down, so an out-of-step blind can be brought to the real
            top and set as fully up there.

    config ROLLO_TOP_OVERRUN_MS
        int "Extra run time past fully up (ms)"
        default 0
        help
            Only if the bottom bar stops against the head and the motor can stall there
            safely: then every move to fully up runs this much longer and corrects the drift
            of time-based positioning. Leave it at 0 if nothing stops the fabric at the top.

    config ROLLO_REVERSE
        bool "Swap motor direction"
        default n
        help
            Same as swapping the two motor wires. The direction can also be swapped over
            Matter, without flashing (the MotorDirectionReversed bit of the Window Covering
            Mode attribute); the two add up.

    config ROLLO_PIN_IN1
        int "GPIO to DRV8833 AIN1"
        default 10

    config ROLLO_PIN_IN2
        int "GPIO to DRV8833 AIN2"
        default 11

    config ROLLO_PIN_SLEEP
        int "GPIO to DRV8833 STBY / nSLEEP"
        default 4

    config ROLLO_LIGHT_SLEEP
        bool "Light-sleep between Thread polls"
        default y
        help
            Saves the battery. Turn it off to rule out sleep problems: the device then stays
            awake (still a sleepy Thread device that polls its parent).

endmenu
